From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 16:18:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 76/98] kernel/vm: validate mmap length/offset (audit MEDIUM)

sys_mmap accepted a zero length, a non-page-aligned file offset, and an
offset+length that wraps past 2^64, passing them into the file-object and
device (/dev/mem) mmap paths.  Reject all three (POSIX EINVAL).  Valid
callers (exec/ld.so map page-aligned segment offsets) are unaffected.

Found by a security audit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/vm/vm_syscalls.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/vm/vm_syscalls.c b/sys/vm/vm_syscalls.c
index 66aaf9c4..d9b9a7e1 100644
--- a/sys/vm/vm_syscalls.c
+++ b/sys/vm/vm_syscalls.c
@@ -243,6 +243,13 @@ void *sys_mmap(void *addr, size_t length, int prot, int flags, int fd, uint64_t
 
     if (vm_round_page_size(length, &aligned_length) != 0) return (void *)-1;
 
+    /* POSIX EINVAL cases that otherwise feed malformed ranges into the
+     * file-object / device (/dev/mem) mmap paths: zero length, a
+     * non-page-aligned file offset, and offset+length wrapping past 2^64. */
+    if (length == 0) return (void *)-1;
+    if (!(flags & MAP_ANONYMOUS) && (offset & 0xFFF)) return (void *)-1;
+    if (offset + (uint64_t)aligned_length < offset) return (void *)-1;
+
     // Find virtual address space
     if (v_addr == 0 || !(flags & MAP_FIXED)) {
         if (vm_map_find_space(map, &v_addr, aligned_length) != 0) return (void *)-1;
